      "end": 2.57,
      "text": "Hello! How's everything today?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 10.17,
      "end": 16.55,
      "text": "It should be, with a bit of preparation. The main risks are a flat battery and tyres getting flat spots."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 19.15,
      "end": 25.99,
      "text": "The easiest option is a trickle charger, which keeps it topped up. If there's no power socket, you could disconnect the negative terminal instead."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 30.51,
      "end": 35.93,
      "text": "Pump them up a little above normal pressure. Fill the fuel tank too, it helps stop moisture building up inside."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 38.5,
      "end": 43.83,
      "text": "For a long stay, it's better to leave it off and chock the wheels or leave it in gear, so the brakes don't stick."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 51.02,
      "end": 57.01,
      "text": "Some insurers offer reduced cover for a car that's off the road. Worth asking, it could save you a bit while you're away."
    }
